n from a single deletion, addressed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be recreated.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan","title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie","title":"Yorkie"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/protoMessageName":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"protoMessageName","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/protoMessageName","title":"protoMessageName","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/protomessagename"}}}